{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK6LeRmG3Y7PLrLeMZxJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed both username validators in `django/contrib/auth/validators.py` so they no longer accept a username that ends with a newline.\n\n- **Change:** `ASCIIUsernameValidator` and `UnicodeUsernameValidator` now use the regex `r'\\A[\\w.@+-]+\\Z'` instead of `r'^[\\w.@+-]+$'`. This is the change the issue suggested. In Python, `$` also matches just before a trailing newline, but `\\Z` only matches at the true end of the string.\n- **Tests:** the existing `auth_tests.test_validators` suite passes (22 tests). I didn't add a test or check a newline-terminated username directly, because test files are off-limits here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":18880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":159},"output_tokens":233,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21206733-e0b4-4423-bc79-f9d35d40fbec","uuid":"227c22fe-6ed1-43a9-846a-c1f479e35d4d","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:45:05.835Z","request_id":"req_011ChK6LeJL3uaPGsNBkFURc"}
